\DOC EXPAND_MAYCHANGE_YMM_REGS_TAC

\TYPE {EXPAND_MAYCHANGE_YMM_REGS_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Rewrites the goal's single {MAYCHANGE}-composition assumption into a normalised
form in which every state component appears in its own one-element {MAYCHANGE},
leaving the conclusion untouched.

\DESCRIBE
The tactic takes no arguments. It acts on a goal whose assumption list contains
exactly one assumption of the form {(MAYCHANGE l1 ,, ... ,, MAYCHANGE ln) s s'}
and replaces it by an equivalent composition in which each {MAYCHANGE} carries
a singleton component list; the register and flag components are reordered
(sorted), duplicated components are merged, and the memory components are
placed last. The conclusion and all other assumptions are unchanged, except
that the rewritten assumption is removed and re-added at the end of the
assumption list, so earlier assumptions shift position.
{
   A, (MAYCHANGE l1 ,, ... ,, MAYCHANGE ln) s s' ?- t
   ==================================================  EXPAND_MAYCHANGE_YMM_REGS_TAC
   A, (MAYCHANGE [c1] ,, ... ,, MAYCHANGE [cm]) s s' ?- t
}

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this one kind of transformation, always on goals
whose conclusion is an {eventually}-style machine-state property and whose
assumptions include exactly one such {MAYCHANGE} term.

\ENDDOC
